Ladybird reads “action” only in manifest version 3 and “browser_action”
only in version 2. All three engines do the same: Chromium’s
_manifest_features.json gives action a min_manifest_version of 3 and
browser_action a max_manifest_version of 2, Gecko’s browser_action.json
schema sets the same limits, and WebKit’s WebExtension reads action when
it supports manifest version 3.
